Software that is "signed" can pass a server-side verification check that Apple performs when a new version of iOS is downloaded. If an update fails the verification check, it can't be installed.<br/>
<br/>
By unsigning software, Apple prevents customers from installing outdated, less secure versions of iOS.<br/>
<br/>
